WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.085
- [Voiceover] All right, go for it.

00:00:03.505 --> 00:00:04.243
(single clap)

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.881
- Ah, what it do, party people?

00:00:09.881 --> 00:00:11.947
Welcome to another episode of Real Mature.

00:00:11.947 --> 00:00:14.153
It's a show that we
make about things you do

00:00:14.153 --> 00:00:15.843
when you grow up, and one of the things

00:00:15.843 --> 00:00:17.887
that happens to you when you grow up is

00:00:17.887 --> 00:00:19.582
the way you party changes.

00:00:19.582 --> 00:00:21.555
So, we have three different stories

00:00:21.555 --> 00:00:24.968
about, well, partying.

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:26.501
The first one involves Keith.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:27.912
- (groans) Let's do this, Henry.

00:00:27.912 --> 00:00:29.190
- (mumbles) Let's get it.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:29.719
All right, let's go!

00:00:29.719 --> 00:00:30.620
Let's go, let's go!

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:31.655
- All right!.

00:00:31.655 --> 00:00:33.559
- [Voiceover] All right, later camera.

00:00:33.559 --> 00:00:37.918
(mellow electronic music)

00:00:39.595 --> 00:00:41.847
- So, today's episode is
about the way you party

00:00:41.847 --> 00:00:44.007
and how it changes as you get older,

00:00:44.007 --> 00:00:46.259
so the first piece is by Keith.

00:00:46.259 --> 00:00:48.743
- Yeah, so for an experiment,
me and my two friends

00:00:48.743 --> 00:00:51.762
who are about 29 and 30
went back to my college

00:00:51.762 --> 00:00:53.062
to try and party like we did

00:00:53.062 --> 00:00:55.720
when we were 20, 21, et cetera.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:56.651
- [Voiceover] Ten-four, that's what

00:00:56.651 --> 00:00:57.528
I was gonna let you know.

00:00:57.528 --> 00:00:59.804
- So, it took (laughs)
us less than 20 seconds

00:00:59.804 --> 00:01:01.615
to get stopped by the police.

00:01:01.615 --> 00:01:03.316
- My name is Brian Wohl.

00:01:03.316 --> 00:01:05.684
I am a handsome 30-year-old man.

00:01:05.684 --> 00:01:06.566
- So, I'm Keith.

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:08.284
I'm a beautiful 27-year-old boy.

00:01:08.284 --> 00:01:09.260
- I'm Marc Muszynksy.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:11.326
I'm 29, looking fine.

00:01:11.326 --> 00:01:14.136
- And I am back at my alma mater.

00:01:14.136 --> 00:01:16.248
- To party like we used
to, see if we can do it,

00:01:16.248 --> 00:01:17.386
see if it's still fun.

00:01:17.386 --> 00:01:18.849
So, we're gonna go pick up Marc.

00:01:18.849 --> 00:01:21.380
Marc I met in college, so
he's gonna get in the car

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:24.561
and he's gonna tell you
about his whole experience.

00:01:24.561 --> 00:01:25.606
- Marc!

00:01:25.606 --> 00:01:26.395
- [Voiceover] Hey.

00:01:26.395 --> 00:01:28.090
- You go take a seat by Henry.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.437
- All right, what's up man?

00:01:29.437 --> 00:01:31.097
- Sitting by you.

00:01:31.097 --> 00:01:32.590
- All right, are you
guys ready to watch this?

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:33.890
- Yeah.
- Let's do it.

00:01:33.890 --> 00:01:34.680
- All right.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:36.584
- So, we used to drink,
like many college students

00:01:36.584 --> 00:01:38.395
are fond of, and we used to play

00:01:38.395 --> 00:01:40.043
a game called "Scepter," or I've heard

00:01:40.043 --> 00:01:41.942
it's also called "Wizard Staff."

00:01:41.942 --> 00:01:45.964
Scepter, where you
would tape the next beer

00:01:45.964 --> 00:01:47.612
to the top of the one you just finished,

00:01:47.612 --> 00:01:49.702
and so as you drank, you'd slowly get

00:01:49.702 --> 00:01:54.253
a longer and longer scepter,
and I am what I think

00:01:54.253 --> 00:01:56.737
is colloquially known as a "wimp,"

00:01:56.737 --> 00:01:58.711
never got one that was more than,

00:01:58.711 --> 00:02:00.708
probably seven was my max.

00:02:00.708 --> 00:02:02.277
- I like how you feel bad about

00:02:02.277 --> 00:02:04.827
having only drank seven beers.
(Marc laughs)

00:02:04.827 --> 00:02:07.845
- So, I think tonight, because
now I'm older and wiser,

00:02:07.845 --> 00:02:09.888
and can think more strategically,

00:02:09.888 --> 00:02:11.258
I think I can get to eight.

00:02:11.258 --> 00:02:12.373
- Can I just say, for the record,

00:02:12.373 --> 00:02:13.627
this is a stupid goal.

00:02:13.627 --> 00:02:15.786
(laughs)
- They're all stupid, Henry.

00:02:15.786 --> 00:02:17.255
None of them are gonna
impress you (laughs).

00:02:17.255 --> 00:02:18.285
(everyone laughs)

00:02:18.285 --> 00:02:21.350
- Five beers, five beers.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:24.299
This scepter has five beers.

00:02:24.299 --> 00:02:25.576
- So, we're on five.

00:02:25.576 --> 00:02:27.457
I was wandering around the party

00:02:27.457 --> 00:02:30.628
doing dramatic, what, in my brain,

00:02:30.628 --> 00:02:33.832
I assume was GoPro party cinematography.

00:02:33.832 --> 00:02:36.608
So, what do you look for
in a party companion?

00:02:38.425 --> 00:02:43.425
- Someone who is rocking
it just as hard as I am.

00:02:43.621 --> 00:02:44.754
- Who's this guy?

00:02:44.754 --> 00:02:47.981
- (laughs) His name is
Brian, but his nickname

00:02:47.981 --> 00:02:50.303
amongst his college friends is "Stick."

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.511
- I mean, he looks glorious.

00:02:51.511 --> 00:02:53.995
- Yeah (laughs), he's an awesome guy.

00:02:53.995 --> 00:02:56.433
- The thing it makes me
think of as a 32-year-old

00:02:56.433 --> 00:02:59.614
is I don't party with
anyone like Stick anymore.

00:02:59.614 --> 00:03:00.589
- Yeah.

00:03:00.589 --> 00:03:02.280
I was able to get to eight beers,

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.964
which is, I guess, my new record.

00:03:04.964 --> 00:03:06.868
- Look how happy you
are with your scepter.

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:09.120
- (laughs) I was thrilled.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:12.579
So, thanks for the swing by memory lane.

00:03:12.579 --> 00:03:13.624
- Ah!

00:03:13.624 --> 00:03:14.623
- Oh no!

00:03:14.623 --> 00:03:16.086
(onlookers laugh)

00:03:16.086 --> 00:03:20.497
- Did going back and partying
like you did 10 years ago

00:03:20.497 --> 00:03:23.469
make you wish you were
still 10 years younger?

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.721
- It made me glad I did it once,

00:03:25.721 --> 00:03:28.856
but it actually just made
me thrilled that I'm not.

00:03:28.856 --> 00:03:31.317
Although those parties are fun,

00:03:31.317 --> 00:03:34.220
when you're done with that lifestyle,

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:37.842
and you go out into a
bigger, more adult world,

00:03:37.842 --> 00:03:40.071
all the rewards for everything
you do during the day

00:03:40.071 --> 00:03:41.622
get so much bigger that that stuff

00:03:41.622 --> 00:03:43.051
is just as fun as partying.

00:03:44.032 --> 00:03:44.974
- That's very grown-up.

00:03:45.885 --> 00:03:48.114
The next video was a
video that I pretty much

00:03:48.114 --> 00:03:50.459
thrust upon our intern, Kane,

00:03:50.459 --> 00:03:52.085
and two of our other interns.

00:03:52.085 --> 00:03:53.431
I brought them into a meeting.

00:03:53.431 --> 00:03:55.126
They didn't know what was gonna happen,

00:03:55.126 --> 00:03:57.680
and I said, "In seven hours, you are going

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.397
"to have a dinner party ready at one

00:04:00.397 --> 00:04:03.787
"of your guys' houses for three

00:04:03.787 --> 00:04:05.737
"of the senior producers on our team."

00:04:05.737 --> 00:04:08.036
- We have no idea what
we're (laughs) gonna do yet.

00:04:08.036 --> 00:04:09.638
- I'm on Pinterest right now

00:04:09.638 --> 00:04:11.310
(Kane laughs)
(mumbles)

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.214
- Going with a California-ish theme.

00:04:13.214 --> 00:04:16.604
- Yeah, the theme is fresh.

00:04:16.604 --> 00:04:18.693
- We spent two hours at Trader Joe's

00:04:18.693 --> 00:04:19.994
looking for stuff.
- We spent two hours

00:04:19.994 --> 00:04:20.969
at Trader Joe's.

00:04:20.969 --> 00:04:22.873
- Okay, so after buying the most random

00:04:22.873 --> 00:04:24.521
assortment of things at Target...

00:04:24.521 --> 00:04:27.234
Can anyone tell me which
one is a serving tray?

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:29.254
I am on my way to Kane's house,

00:04:29.254 --> 00:04:30.634
and we're gonna do this thing.

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:32.750
- All right, we're starting to cook now.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:34.584
We have all our stuff ready.

00:04:34.584 --> 00:04:36.093
We moved the table down.

00:04:36.093 --> 00:04:38.382
(acoustic blues music)

00:04:38.382 --> 00:04:40.170
- I think we started off slow.

00:04:40.170 --> 00:04:41.679
We did take a 20-minute nap earlier

00:04:41.679 --> 00:04:43.328
