to join me, and just make
the whole event about me.

00:09:28.544 --> 00:09:30.796
Who will play us in beer pong?

00:09:30.796 --> 00:09:34.900
(high-pitched, sped-up talking)

00:09:38.063 --> 00:09:39.526
- BWo's having a good time.

00:09:39.526 --> 00:09:41.575
- Behind your back.
- Do it again.

00:09:41.575 --> 00:09:44.268
(group cheers)

00:09:44.268 --> 00:09:46.807
- Did you care what the college students

00:09:46.807 --> 00:09:48.526
thought of you as you were partying?

00:09:48.526 --> 00:09:52.217
- I wanted to have the most fun possible,

00:09:52.217 --> 00:09:54.353
and generally, having
the most fun possible

00:09:54.353 --> 00:09:58.648
is getting as many people
together to share that fun.

00:09:58.648 --> 00:09:59.467
- [Voiceover] All right, Bwo.

00:09:59.467 --> 00:10:00.628
How are you feeling?

00:10:00.628 --> 00:10:02.230
- I'm all right.

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:03.809
I haven't had my coffee yet.

00:10:03.809 --> 00:10:05.918
- Who's this bearded
man in the background?

00:10:05.918 --> 00:10:06.893
- I was wondering when you guys

00:10:06.893 --> 00:10:08.913
would notice the naked man in the bed.

00:10:08.913 --> 00:10:09.652
- Who's that?
- Yeah, is this

00:10:09.652 --> 00:10:10.859
the first time you've found him?

00:10:10.859 --> 00:10:14.853
- I was able to achieve
my goals, just about.

00:10:14.853 --> 00:10:18.150
I got everybody to chant some things.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:21.137
(unintelligible shouting)

00:10:21.137 --> 00:10:23.926
- [All together] Down the pipes!

00:10:23.926 --> 00:10:27.084
- We were able to sing
some songs at the party.

00:10:27.084 --> 00:10:29.615
- [Voiceover] Goodbye
gray skies, hello blue!

00:10:29.615 --> 00:10:30.776
Oh wait, we can't sing that song.

00:10:30.776 --> 00:10:31.635
It's copyrighted.

00:10:31.635 --> 00:10:32.541
(laughs)

00:10:32.541 --> 00:10:34.955
- Got a dance party
going, so that was good.

00:10:34.955 --> 00:10:35.954
I'm staying.

00:10:35.954 --> 00:10:36.813
- [Voiceover] Staying in college?

00:10:36.813 --> 00:10:37.509
- Yeah.

00:10:37.509 --> 00:10:38.415
- [Voiceover] You'll keep partying here?

00:10:38.415 --> 00:10:39.042
- Yeah.

00:10:39.042 --> 00:10:39.622
- [Voiceover] Into it?

00:10:39.622 --> 00:10:40.203
- Yeah.

00:10:40.203 --> 00:10:40.830
- [Voiceover] Nice.

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:41.689
- I'm just staying.

00:10:41.689 --> 00:10:43.483
- [Voiceover] Great, that's cool.

00:10:43.483 --> 00:10:44.893
- He's staying.

00:10:44.893 --> 00:10:45.673
- Wait, wait.

00:10:45.673 --> 00:10:46.602
Is that Stick?

00:10:46.602 --> 00:10:47.600
- Yeah (laughs).
- That's Stick.

00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:48.366
- We love Stick.

00:10:48.366 --> 00:10:50.526
You know, Stick is like
this super party bro,

00:10:50.526 --> 00:10:53.869
but he's also the sweetest
man at that school.

00:10:53.869 --> 00:10:55.889
- He looks like Zac Efron in Neighbors.

00:10:55.889 --> 00:10:56.934
(laughs)

00:10:56.934 --> 00:10:59.233
- I got the Maui Wowie,
which has jalapenos,

00:10:59.233 --> 00:11:02.042
ham, cheese, and pineapple.

00:11:02.042 --> 00:11:05.107
I had such a great time eating that food.

00:11:05.107 --> 00:11:06.106
It's fabulous.

00:11:06.106 --> 00:11:07.220
Very real.

00:11:07.220 --> 00:11:10.652
But this morning, I am feeling that food.

00:11:10.652 --> 00:11:12.417
- [Voiceover] How did you
feel at the end of the night?

00:11:12.417 --> 00:11:15.203
Like, successful, tired?

00:11:15.203 --> 00:11:17.014
- I felt incredibly successful.

00:11:17.014 --> 00:11:18.245
- At this point, we've outlasted

00:11:18.245 --> 00:11:20.218
most of the actual college students.

00:11:20.218 --> 00:11:21.077
- Yeah.

00:11:21.077 --> 00:11:21.681
- That's great.

00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:23.092
You guys outlasted the college students?

00:11:23.092 --> 00:11:23.835
- Yeah, man.

00:11:23.835 --> 00:11:25.995
- Do you want to party like this more

00:11:25.995 --> 00:11:27.373
now that you've had a taste of it?

00:11:28.376 --> 00:11:30.388
- Absolutely not.

00:11:30.388 --> 00:11:32.040
No, no.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:34.976
- All right, we'll go
on to the next segment.

00:11:34.976 --> 00:11:37.461
Who here knows who Andrew W.K. is?

00:11:38.361 --> 00:11:39.479
- I do.

00:11:39.479 --> 00:11:42.474
- Andrew W.K. is a rock musician.

00:11:42.474 --> 00:11:43.333
He's turned himself into the world's

00:11:43.333 --> 00:11:45.377
foremost authority on partying,

00:11:45.377 --> 00:11:48.465
but he almost a philosophy of partying.

00:11:48.465 --> 00:11:50.833
So, we asked our friend,
comedian Greg Barris,

00:11:50.833 --> 00:11:53.615
to interview him at the
Everything Is festival

00:11:53.615 --> 00:11:55.449
in Portland a couple weeks ago,

00:11:55.449 --> 00:11:58.746
and find out some of his
amazing rules for partying.

00:11:58.746 --> 00:12:01.091
- Hey, it's Greg Barris for BuzzFeed.

00:12:01.091 --> 00:12:02.600
You know, from the internet,

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:06.106
talking with Andrew W.K.
about partying as an adult.

00:12:06.106 --> 00:12:07.360
- Hello, how are you?

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:08.423
- I'm doing good, how you doing?

00:12:08.423 --> 00:12:09.422
- Fine, thank you.

00:12:09.422 --> 00:12:11.279
- How did you become
an expert on partying?

00:12:11.279 --> 00:12:13.485
- Well, by doing it primarily,

00:12:13.485 --> 00:12:15.877
by engaging in a celebratory mindset,

00:12:15.877 --> 00:12:19.963
but primarily, you can declare yourself

00:12:19.963 --> 00:12:22.866
to take on an endeavor, so I said,

00:12:22.866 --> 00:12:25.652
"I wanna be good at partying,"

00:12:25.652 --> 00:12:28.392
and so, lo and behold, I was.

00:12:28.392 --> 00:12:29.947
- Why'd you pick partying?

00:12:29.947 --> 00:12:31.480
- To get cheered up.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:33.198
- Oh, so you were un-cheered.

00:12:33.198 --> 00:12:35.116
- I struggled with that consistently.

00:12:35.116 --> 00:12:36.695
I definitely wanted to cheer myself up.

00:12:36.695 --> 00:12:38.993
This partying mindset has helped

00:12:38.993 --> 00:12:41.362
with that a great deal, and it's been

00:12:41.362 --> 00:12:43.343
the motivation for my life mission.

00:12:45.062 --> 00:12:47.379
I don't want to say it
kills two, but it flutters

00:12:47.379 --> 00:12:50.212
two birds with one gust of wind.

00:12:50.212 --> 00:12:51.210
- That is beautiful.

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:51.860
- Thank you.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:53.393
- Am I too old to party?

00:12:53.393 --> 00:12:54.531
- Well, no.

00:12:54.531 --> 00:12:56.179
I would only say someone would be too old

00:12:56.179 --> 00:12:58.919
if there's parts of their physique

00:12:58.919 --> 00:13:01.125
which has grown decrepit, but even then,

00:13:01.125 --> 00:13:03.632
partying can actually
help bolster the body.

00:13:03.632 --> 00:13:05.536
If you're 99 years old, and your body

00:13:05.536 --> 00:13:07.719
has grown decrepit and withered,

00:13:07.719 --> 00:13:08.671
for example, there was a gentlemen

00:13:08.671 --> 00:13:10.784
on the airplane today
that had two crutches,

00:13:10.784 --> 00:13:14.081
and he was quite elderly, but
he was still hardy in spirit,

00:13:14.081 --> 00:13:16.798
so his partying may be less physical

00:13:16.798 --> 00:13:18.957
and more spirit-based, and then someone

00:13:18.957 --> 00:13:21.488
like a young child who is only scampering,

00:13:21.488 --> 00:13:23.392
and whose soul hasn't
developed that much yet

00:13:23.392 --> 00:13:24.878
because they haven't lived that long,

00:13:24.878 --> 00:13:26.201
at least in this embodiment,

00:13:26.201 --> 00:13:28.943
maybe they're a more physical party.

00:13:28.943 --> 00:13:30.627
- Yeah.
- They're just running amok.

00:13:30.627 --> 00:13:32.275
- So, like I'm in my thirties,

00:13:32.275 --> 00:13:35.456
I get tired easily, I can't
party like the way I used to.

00:13:35.456 --> 00:13:39.310
What are some ways to
combat party fatigue?

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:42.445
- Well actually, being
fatigued can count as partying.

00:13:42.445 --> 00:13:44.496
- Oh.
- So, resting...

00:13:44.496 --> 00:13:45.969
- Oh, okay.
- Sitting,

00:13:45.969 --> 00:13:47.409
like you're doing now, laying.

00:13:47.409 --> 00:13:48.338
- Napping.

00:13:48.338 --> 00:13:50.172
- Napping, but nap hard.

00:13:50.172 --> 00:13:52.749
- For people with a more
conventional lifestyle,

00:13:52.749 --> 00:13:55.744
like a day job, how do they integrate

00:13:55.744 --> 00:13:59.245
partying into that lifestyle?

00:13:59.245 --> 00:14:02.287
- You have usually eight hours of work,

00:14:02.287 --> 00:14:04.237
hopefully that you can
take some kind of pride in.

00:14:04.237 --> 00:14:06.072
Even if you hate the
job, you can still try

00:14:06.072 --> 00:14:08.533
to do a good job at what you hate.

00:14:08.533 --> 00:14:12.782
Eight hours of rest, or
some version of that,

00:14:12.782 --> 00:14:14.477
and then you hope to have eight hours

00:14:14.477 --> 00:14:18.946
to kind of do whatever else,
and that's the precious time.

00:14:18.946 --> 00:14:21.406
So really, if you only have that precious

00:14:21.406 --> 00:14:24.610
eight hours of your life,
you can make that count,

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:29.349
and really, really sort
of live in that slice,

00:14:29.349 --> 00:14:31.980
that third, or something.

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:33.247
- Or something.

00:14:33.247 --> 00:14:34.222
- Always "or something."

00:14:34.222 --> 00:14:35.374
- Yeah, there's more
something all the time.

00:14:35.374 --> 00:14:35.991
- Always.

00:14:36.739 --> 00:14:37.761
- That was pretty cool.

00:14:37.761 --> 00:14:38.806
- Yeah, pretty good.

00:14:38.806 --> 00:14:41.987
- So, are you ready to
watch your party experience?

00:14:41.987 --> 00:14:43.682
- Sure, I edited it, so I know what it is.

00:14:43.682 --> 00:14:44.610
Let's watch it (laughs).

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:45.493
- Okay.

00:14:45.493 --> 00:14:46.677
- One of the objectives I have

00:14:46.677 --> 00:14:49.621
is to play beer pong, and
win a game of beer pong.

00:14:49.621 --> 00:14:51.920
I will have to play beer pong until I win,

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:53.959
because I used to win.

00:14:53.959 --> 00:14:56.052
I haven't played beer pong in a long time.

00:14:56.712 --> 00:14:57.687
- [Voiceover] They're chugging beers.

00:14:57.687 --> 00:14:58.616
- We're doing it.

00:14:58.616 --> 00:15:03.186
(high-pitched, sped-up talking)

00:15:06.362 --> 00:15:07.732
- Good little montage.

00:15:07.732 --> 00:15:10.356
Are you embarrassed by how important

00:15:10.356 --> 00:15:12.399
beer pong is to you?

00:15:12.399 --> 00:15:13.908
- I used to win beer pong all the time.

00:15:13.908 --> 00:15:15.766
I built my own beer pong table.

00:15:15.766 --> 00:15:17.229
It was called "The Floorboard,"

00:15:17.229 --> 00:15:18.751
because I made it out of flooring.

00:15:19.337 --> 00:15:21.027
Oh, well, we did it.

00:15:21.027 --> 00:15:24.324
We got back at 4:00, or 3:45.

00:15:24.324 --> 00:15:25.647
It was a crazy night.

00:15:25.647 --> 00:15:29.376
We played beer pong, lost the first game.

00:15:30.802 --> 00:15:31.869
- Damn it!

00:15:31.869 --> 00:15:33.889
- Oh!
- Mother fucker!

00:15:33.889 --> 00:15:35.398
You gotta be kidding me!

00:15:35.398 --> 00:15:38.486
- Me and BWo really
embraced the true nature

00:15:38.486 --> 00:15:41.203
of beer pong, which is
to say something together

00:15:41.203 --> 00:15:44.082
with your partner every
time you're about to shoot.

00:15:44.082 --> 00:15:45.661
Somehow it gets you in the zone.

00:15:45.661 --> 00:15:46.287
(cheers off-screen)

00:15:46.287 --> 00:15:47.161
- You did it.

00:15:47.161 --> 00:15:48.507
I won a game of beer pong.

00:15:48.507 --> 00:15:49.274
- [Voiceover] Finally!

00:15:49.274 --> 00:15:50.663
- We won.

00:15:50.663 --> 00:15:52.301
- For us to win, we had to go,

00:15:52.301 --> 00:15:55.296
(together) "Octavarius, so nefarious."

00:15:55.296 --> 00:15:57.687
- And it's also about the
power of touch, Henry.

00:15:57.687 --> 00:15:58.746
It unites people.

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:02.206
(everyone laughs)

00:16:02.206 --> 00:16:04.611
- Okay (mumbles).

00:16:07.147 --> 00:16:10.560
- Me and Mark tried to chug a beer

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:11.930
faster than a girl.

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:14.182
- Yeah!
- Yeah, chug!

00:16:14.182 --> 00:16:16.657
(everyone cheers)

00:16:17.638 --> 00:16:19.008
- Couldn't.

00:16:19.008 --> 00:16:21.399
Both college students beat both of us

00:16:21.399 --> 00:16:22.398
in the chugging contest.

00:16:22.398 --> 00:16:24.274
Mark didn't even try.

00:16:24.274 --> 00:16:26.526
Mark just didn't try.

00:16:26.526 --> 00:16:29.099
We went to four-square,

00:16:29.099 --> 00:16:31.467
and in four-square, I fell down,

00:16:31.467 --> 00:16:32.651
got a little cut there.

00:16:32.651 --> 00:16:33.998
- It's funny how often you get hurt

00:16:33.998 --> 00:16:36.808
while drinking when
you're young versus now.

00:16:36.808 --> 00:16:38.131
I never get hurt.

00:16:38.131 --> 00:16:39.431
- Yeah, because when
you're young and drinking,

00:16:39.431 --> 00:16:41.660
you have so much more energy to go out

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:44.075
and attack the world,
where now if I'm drinking,

00:16:44.075 --> 00:16:46.002
I'm like, "I'm cool to sit on this stool."

00:16:46.002 --> 00:16:46.629
- Yeah.

00:16:46.629 --> 00:16:47.860
I don't feel invincible anymore.

00:16:47.860 --> 00:16:48.928
- Yeah.

00:16:48.928 --> 00:16:51.668
But today, we're pretty hung over.

00:16:51.668 --> 00:16:53.177
We're gonna go eat some shepherd's pie

00:16:53.177 --> 00:16:54.199
at an Irish pub.

00:16:55.879 --> 00:16:56.960
That's it, right?

00:16:57.732 --> 00:16:58.962
Did we do it?

00:16:58.962 --> 00:17:00.541
(mumbles)

00:17:00.541 --> 00:17:04.928
(everyone laughs)

00:17:04.928 --> 00:17:06.410
- Yeah, so now we're getting tacos

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:08.300
at my favorite taco stand.

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:09.461
- [Voiceover] Did anything
about this experience

00:17:09.461 --> 00:17:11.875
make you guys sad?

00:17:11.875 --> 00:17:13.129
- The thing that I miss the most

00:17:13.129 --> 00:17:15.753
about college is the
immediacy of all your friends,

00:17:15.753 --> 00:17:20.141
how easy it is for 25
people that you really love

00:17:20.141 --> 00:17:22.324
to just show up in 10 minutes.

00:17:22.324 --> 00:17:23.903
So, that's pretty much it, you know?

00:17:23.903 --> 00:17:24.785
We went down.

00:17:24.785 --> 00:17:26.178
We all had pretty much the same time.

00:17:26.178 --> 00:17:27.548
We had a lot of fun, but ultimately

00:17:27.548 --> 00:17:30.102
we like partying how
we already party here,

00:17:30.102 --> 00:17:31.774
which, really, is similar.

00:17:31.774 --> 00:17:33.562
We get drunk, but we just
don't stay out as late

00:17:33.562 --> 00:17:36.627
and we don't drink to
incredible excess anymore.

00:17:36.627 --> 00:17:37.672
- Yeah.
- I feel like we've found

00:17:37.672 --> 00:17:39.924
the highlights of what this can be,

00:17:39.924 --> 00:17:42.223
and then we do those to
the best of our ability.

00:17:42.223 --> 00:17:45.404
- That's how you party as
you get older, I guess.

00:17:45.404 --> 00:17:47.052
- Plus, fucking tacos for days.

00:17:47.052 --> 00:17:48.190
- Yeah, tacos for days.

00:17:48.190 --> 00:17:49.583
- Tacos for days.

00:17:49.583 --> 00:17:51.742
- Know that, and thanks
for watching Real Mature.

00:17:51.742 --> 00:17:53.159
Until next time.

00:17:53.159 --> 00:17:54.714
What it do.
- What it do.

00:17:54.714 --> 00:17:55.702
- [all together] What it do!

